Added opt-in `events_keys` values `"storage"` and `"contract_calls"` (not in `"*"`). Observers that set them receive a `vm_events` array on `POST /new_block` for committed Clarity `var-set` / map writes and nested `contract-call?` (including `define-data-var` initializers). Collection uses the VM eval-hook path and is off unless an observer opts in. Array order is the index; these events do not use `event_index`. Per-tx RAM cap `[node] vm_trace_max_bytes` defaults to `0` (unlimited). A positive value is an emergency brake that emits `type: "truncated"` and drops the rest of that tx's traces — do not set it on a genesis feeder that reconstructs Clarity state.
